--- 8.2 Predictability of early citations ---

Predictability of log(early citations) -- share of variance explained:
  Journal+year+topic FE only      : R2 = 0.110
  + article observables           : R2 = 0.222
  + author quality (N=724)        : R2 = 0.243
  -> fundamentals explain ~22% of early-citation variation.

--- 8.3 Decomposition of early citations ---

Propagation of the explained vs unexplained component (long-run outcome):
  explained component  : 1.068 (robust SE 0.054)
  unexplained component: 0.770 (robust SE 0.020)
  SD(unexplained) = 0.796 -> a 1-SD shock = 85% more long-run citations.

  [growth outcome] explained  : 1.014 (rse 0.063 )
  [growth outcome] unexplained: 0.653 (rse 0.024 )

